{"parentUuid":"218e7142-7dd7-448a-91cc-0fdcdcd068ff","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a2dc46b9af8a17e14","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01BViYmpZzY3YUSc5ivKquL3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017eguqmTwSSzUbd6SfUFkJE","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"CP-SAT linearization extension hint warm start LP cuts add_linear_constraint custom inequality"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4332,"cache_read_input_tokens":25123,"output_tokens":282,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4332},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":282,"cache_read_input_tokens":25123,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4332,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4332,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caoza2QLbCXZdf7gezrgZ","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"d7a5a998-8fff-4826-a9ba-41b20934723f","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:25:26.109Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"d7a5a998-8fff-4826-a9ba-41b20934723f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a2dc46b9af8a17e14","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017eguqmTwSSzUbd6SfUFkJE","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT linearization extension hint warm start LP cuts add_linear_constraint custom inequality\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT for scheduling Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://schedulingseminar.com/presentations/SchedulingSeminar_LaurentPerron.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"How does it work? - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding CP-SAT: Constraint Programming Meets SAT Solving | by Jonas Poelmans | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@jonaspoelmans120/understanding-cp-sat-constraint-programming-meets-sat-solving-b137dddb943c\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT, UNKNOWN status with complete solution hint · Issue #3750 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3750\"},{\"title\":\"LinearProgrammingConstraint | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/reference/sat/linear_programming_constraint/LinearProgrammingConstraint\"},{\"title\":\"MIP aspects of OR-tools CP-SAT solver. Frederic Didier (fdid@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://www.mixedinteger.org/EUROMIP/2025/slides/frederic-didier.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"}]\n\nThe search results provide information about CP-SAT's handling of linear constraints, LP relaxations, and warm starts. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Linear Constraints and LP Integration\n\nThe `LinearProgrammingConstraint` class manages linear programming within a constraint satisfaction context, with key actions including adding linear constraints (`AddLinearConstraint`), registering cut generators (`AddCutGenerator`), and setting objective coefficients (`SetObjectiveCoefficient`).\n\n## Warm Start and LP Cuts\n\nThe optimal linear relaxation may be computed through warm-starts utilized deeper down the search tree, and at root level, cutting planes such as Gomory-Cuts are applied to improve the linear relaxation.\n\n## Solution Hints\n\nWhen available, solution hints should be provided—for example, in daily replanning where yesterday's solution is available, use it as a hint. The solver doesn't blindly trust hints but uses them to focus initial search on promising regions.\n\n## Custom Constraints and Integer Requirements\n\nAll constraints in CP-SAT must be defined using integers; multiply by a large integer if necessary to convert non-integer terms. This applies to custom inequality constraints as well.\n\nThe search results show that CP-SAT integrates linear programming relaxations, cutting planes, and warm-start mechanisms to enhance its constraint programming approach, though the specific implementation details for custom linearization hints may be found in the Google OR-Tools documentation.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"d53673c4-0efd-45a4-b913-309671e7b711","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:25:32.837Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d7a5a998-8fff-4826-a9ba-41b20934723f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"b34b69a9-344d-4a5d-bccb-99ee5a8fffa7","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a2dc46b9af8a17e14","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FZjiXEmzNDK92iU8SRazTu","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"RLT level-1 RLT-1 RLT-2 hierarchy quadratic assignment QAP rectangle packing LP relaxation tightness\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"An LP-based characterization of solvable QAP instances with chess-board and graded structures | Journal of Combinatorial Optimization | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10878-023-01044-3\"},{\"title\":\"Symmetry in RLT-type relaxations for the quadratic assignment and standard quadratic optimization problems - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0377221713008308\"},{\"title\":\"Strong RLT1 bounds from decomposable Lagrangean relaxation for some quadratic 0–1 optimization problems with linear constraints | Annals of Operations Research\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10479-018-3092-8\"},{\"title\":\"RLT2-BASED PARALLEL ALGORITHMS FOR SOLVING LARGE QUADRATIC\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1710.03732\"},{\"title\":\"Strong RLT1 bounds from decomposable Lagrangean relaxation for some quadratic 0–1 optimization problems with linear constraints\",\"url\":\"https://ideas.repec.org/a/spr/annopr/v286y2020i1d10.1007_s10479-018-3092-8.html\"},{\"title\":\"Symmetry in RLT-type relaxations for the quadratic assignment and standard quadratic optimization problems\",\"url\":\"https://ideas.repec.org/a/eee/ejores/v233y2014i3p488-499.html\"},{\"title\":\"Symmetry in RLT-type relaxations for the quadratic assignment ...\",\"url\":\"https://optimization-online.org/wp-content/uploads/2012/01/3303.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"An LP-based characterization of solvable QAP instances with chess-board and graded structures\",\"url\":\"https://ideas.repec.org/a/spr/jcomop/v45y2023i5d10.1007_s10878-023-01044-3.html\"},{\"title\":\"A Graphics Processing Unit Algorithm to Solve the Quadratic Assignment Problem Using Level-2 Reformulation-Linearization Technique | INFORMS Journal on Computing\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/abs/10.1287/ijoc.2017.0754\"},{\"title\":\"A revised reformulation-linearization technique for the quadratic assignment problem | Discrete Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/abs/10.1016/j.disopt.2014.08.003\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found substantial information about RLT (Reformulation-Linearization Technique) levels, QAP (Quadratic Assignment Problem), and LP relaxation tightness. Here's a summary of the key findings:\n\n## RLT Hierarchy and QAP\n\nThe Reformulation Linearization Technique (RLT) when applied to a pure 0–1 quadratic optimization problem constructs a hierarchy of LP models of increasing sizes that provide monotonically improving continuous bounds on the optimal value as the level increases.\n\n## RLT Levels (RLT-1, RLT-2, RLT-3)\n\nThe most promising formulation for QAP was obtained by Adams and Johnson (1994) by applying level-1 reformulation and linearization technique (RLT1) to the QAP, which yielded strong LP relaxation bounds. \n\nThe second level RLT relaxation of the QAP often provides significantly better bounds than the first level RLT relaxation, but it is computationally very expensive to solve. The third level RLT relaxation of the QAP was also investigated, and the numerical results show that this relaxation empirically provides tight bounds for medium-sized instances.\n\n## LP Relaxation Tightness\n\nThe objective function value of the LP relaxation of RLT2 was shown to provide tight lower bounds equal to the integer optimal for small QAPs (n ≤12). RLT2 and RLT3 formulations provide much stronger lower bounds compared to RLT1, and for many problem instances they are able to match the optimal objective value of the QAP.\n\nThe search results focus on the QAP, but do not contain specific information about rectangle packing problems in relation to RLT hierarchies.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"2c8022cb-c027-4787-8828-ea6ca9da5de2","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:25:34.013Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b34b69a9-344d-4a5d-bccb-99ee5a8fffa7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"218e7142-7dd7-448a-91cc-0fdcdcd068ff","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a2dc46b9af8a17e14","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NYtQt3tHqPLwnKaBc8T7Wz","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"Lodi\" OR \"Monaci\" OR \"Sherali\" 2D rectangle packing reformulation linearization MIP relaxation\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"(PDF) The Two Dimensional Bin Packing Problem with Side Constraints\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/312919075_The_Two_Dimensional_Bin_Packing_Problem_with_Side_Constraints\"},{\"title\":\"Exact Solution Techniques for Two-dimensional Cutting and Packing\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/am/pii/S0377221720306111\"},{\"title\":\"The two-dimensional bin packing problem with variable bin sizes and costs - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1572528605000216\"},{\"title\":\"Positions and covering: A two-stage methodology to obtain optimal solutions for the 2d-bin packing problem | PLOS One\",\"url\":\"https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371%2Fjournal.pone.0229358\"},{\"title\":\"Two-dimensional packing problems: A survey | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/4870246_Two-dimensional_packing_problems_A_survey\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - ktnr/BinPacking2D: Exact solutions for two-dimensional bin packing problems by branch-and-cut · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ktnr/BinPacking2D\"},{\"title\":\"Frontiers | Two-dimensional irregular packing problems: A review\",\"url\":\"https://www.frontiersin.org/articles/10.3389/fmech.2022.966691\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Solving the 2D Bin Packing Problem by Means of a Hybrid Evolutionary Algorithm\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/257720044_Solving_the_2D_Bin_Packing_Problem_by_Means_of_a_Hybrid_Evolutionary_Algorithm\"},{\"title\":\"dblp: Michele Monaci\",\"url\":\"https://dblp.org/pers/m/Monaci:Michele.html\"},{\"title\":\"Transformer-based placement heuristic for online 2D strip packing problem - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0360835225006102\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about work by Lodi and Monaci on 2D rectangle packing problems. However, the search didn't return specific results about \"reformulation linearization\" or \"MIP relaxation\" in combination with these authors. Let me search more specifically for those terms.\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Reformulation–Linearization Techniques for Discrete Optimization Problems | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/rwe/10.1007/978-1-4419-7997-1_45\"},{\"title\":\"Reformulation-Linearization Technique for Global Optimization | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/rwe/10.1007/978-0-387-74759-0_559\"},{\"title\":\"Reformulation‐Linearization Technique for MIPs - Sherali - 2011 - Major Reference Works - Wiley Online Library\",\"url\":\"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/abs/10.1002/9780470400531.eorms0712\"},{\"title\":\"Reformulation-Linearization Methods for Global Optimization | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/rwe/10.1007/0-306-48332-7_426\"},{\"title\":\"A Reformulation-Linearization Technique for Solving Discrete and Continuous Nonconvex Problems | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-1-4757-4388-3\"},{\"title\":\"LP-based approximations for disjoint bilinear and two-stage adjustable robust optimization | Mathematical Programming | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10107-023-02004-9\"},{\"title\":\"A new reformulation-linearization technique for bilinear programming problems | Journal of Global Optimization | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF00122429\"},{\"title\":\"A Reformulation-Linearization Technique (RLT) for semi-infinite and convex programs under mixed 0-1 and general discrete restrictions - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0166218X08002011\"},{\"title\":\"Reformulation–Linearization Techniques for Mixed-Discrete Optimization Problems | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/rwe/10.1007/978-1-4614-6624-6_45-1\"},{\"title\":\"Reformulation‐Linearization Technique for MIPs | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/319371127_Reformulation-Linearization_Technique_for_MIPs\"}]\n\nBased on my search results, I found relevant information about both the authors you mentioned and reformulation-linearization techniques, though I couldn't find a single publication combining all three names with the specific focus on 2D rectangle packing.\n\n## Summary of Findings:\n\n### Lodi and Monaci's Work on 2D Rectangle Packing\n\nPolynomial formulations for 2-staged guillotine packing were proposed by Lodi and Monaci for the 2D-KP and by Lodi, Martello, and Vigo for the 2D-BPP and the 2D-SPP. Lodi and Monaci also developed partial enumeration algorithms for the Two-Dimensional Bin Packing Problem with guillotine constraints.\n\n### Sherali's Reformulation-Linearization Technique (RLT)\n\nThe reformulation-linearization technique (RLT) for mixed-integer programs is an automatic model enhancement approach that generates a hierarchy of relaxations spanning the spectrum from the continuous linear programming relaxation to the convex hull of feasible solutions, applicable to both 0-1 as well as general discrete programs, and often, the first-level relaxation itself provides a sufficiently tight model reformulation that significantly improves problem solvability.\n\nRLT describes the reformulation–linearization technique for solving mixed-integer 0-1 and general mixed-discrete optimization problems, and the use of RLT for directly lifting mixed-integer programs (MIPs) into higher-dimensional representations as well as for deriving strong valid inequalities in the space of the original variables.\n\nWhile both Lodi/Monaci and Sherali have significant contributions to packing problems and MIP techniques respectively, I could not find a specific joint publication that combines these authors' work on 2D rectangle packing with reformulation-linearization and MIP relaxation in a single paper.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"70380f52-c117-4dd1-b935-b07414db464d","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:25:46.212Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"218e7142-7dd7-448a-91cc-0fdcdcd068ff","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
