{"parentUuid":"eca67c23-f9af-4649-b3b2-db7f0940f9a1","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a2dc46b9af8a17e14","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Tsb7fKVeeZTBCeuYRs72Kh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Uw2z4rhgUvYWi8hGjSZgdo","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"Gurobi RLT preprocessing automatic linearization bilinear product variable improvement"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1383,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4210,"cache_read_input_tokens":29455,"output_tokens":181,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4210},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1383,"output_tokens":181,"cache_read_input_tokens":29455,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4210,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4210,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaozbvyxocUjBm3UQ8Twp","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"2e6f8e50-4680-405f-8e37-b062ae87f740","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:25:49.810Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"eca67c23-f9af-4649-b3b2-db7f0940f9a1","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a2dc46b9af8a17e14","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012pCN8s6AZquTiitGKAkNPu","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"reformulation linearization\" valid inequality preprocessing strengthening mixed integer programming 2024 2025 packing scheduling\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Reformulation–Linearization Techniques for Mixed-Discrete Optimization Problems | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/rwe/10.1007/978-1-4614-6624-6_45-1\"},{\"title\":\"Reformulation–Linearization Techniques for Discrete Optimization Problems | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/rwe/10.1007/978-1-4419-7997-1_45\"},{\"title\":\"Solving Mixed Integer Programming Problems Using Automatic Reformulation | Operations Research\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/opre.35.1.45\"},{\"title\":\"Mixed Integer Programming Workshop 2025\",\"url\":\"https://www.mixedinteger.org/2025/\"},{\"title\":\"A reformulation strategy for mixed-integer linear bi-level programming problems | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/352482885_A_reformulation_strategy_for_mixed-integer_linear_bi-level_programming_problems\"},{\"title\":\"Mixed Integer Linear Programming Formulation Techniques\",\"url\":\"https://juan-pablo-vielma.github.io/publications/Mixed-Integer-Linear-Programming-Formulation-Techniques.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Tight Relaxations for Nonconvex Optimization Problems Using the Reformulation-Linearization/Convexification Technique (RLT) | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-1-4757-5362-2_1\"},{\"title\":\"MILP Solvers: Methods and Advances\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/mixed-integer-linear-programming-milp-solvers\"},{\"title\":\"Last fifty years of integer linear programming: A focus on recent practical advances - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0377221724008877\"},{\"title\":\"Reformulations in Mathematical Programming: A Computational Approach\",\"url\":\"https://www.lix.polytechnique.fr/~liberti/arschapter.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here's what I found regarding reformulation linearization, valid inequalities, preprocessing, and strengthening in mixed integer programming:\n\n## Reformulation-Linearization Techniques (RLT)\n\nRLT is used for directly lifting mixed-integer programs (MIPs) into higher-dimensional representations as well as for deriving strong valid inequalities in the space of the original variables. The principal RLT construct for such problems is to first reformulate the problem by adding a suitable set of polynomial constraints and then to linearize this resulting problem through a variable substitution process in order to produce a tight higher dimensional linear programming relaxation.\n\n## Recent 2024-2025 Developments\n\nRecent work includes \"Characterizing linearizable QAPs by the Level-1 reformulation-linearization technique\" (2024), and Sherali, Adams and colleagues published \"Reformulation–Linearization Techniques for Mixed-Discrete Optimization Problems\" (2025).\n\n## Valid Inequalities and Strengthening\n\nVarious additional classes of valid inequalities, filtered through a constraint selection scheme or a separation routine, are proposed to further tighten the developed relaxation while keeping it manageable in size. Cutting plane methods tighten relaxations by introducing valid linear inequalities (\"cuts\") to separate fractional solutions (Zhang et al., 2024).\n\n## Preprocessing and Formulation Strengthening\n\nThe initial formulation provided by the user is automatically simplified and improved with a sizable variety of pre-processing steps which attempt to reduce the number of variables and constraints. At each node of the Branch-and-Bound algorithm, the formulation may be tightened as needed by inserting and removing additional valid constraints.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"d36330e2-ebeb-4e27-b447-c271830b30d9","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:25:56.831Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"eca67c23-f9af-4649-b3b2-db7f0940f9a1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"2e6f8e50-4680-405f-8e37-b062ae87f740","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a2dc46b9af8a17e14","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Uw2z4rhgUvYWi8hGjSZgdo","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Gurobi RLT preprocessing automatic linearization bilinear product variable improvement\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Products of Variables in Mixed Integer Programming - Gurobi Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://www.gurobi.com/events/products-of-variables-in-mixed-integer-programming/\"},{\"title\":\"bilinear transformation and GRB.Param.NonConvex – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/community/posts/12159753128593-bilinear-transformation-and-GRB-Param-NonConvex\"},{\"title\":\"Specialized Strategies for Products of Binary Variables\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.gurobi.com/wp-content/uploads/Models-with-Products-of-Binary-Variables.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Question about linearization – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/community/posts/14695552377361-Question-about-linearization-\"},{\"title\":\"Linearize quadratic continuous constraints – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/community/posts/360077004552-Linearize-quadratic-continuous-constraints\"},{\"title\":\"Gurobi Events & Webinars\",\"url\":\"https://stage.gurobi.com/events/products-of-variables-in-mixed-integer-programming/\"},{\"title\":\"Efficient separation of RLT cuts for implicit and explicit bilinear terms | Mathematical Programming | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10107-024-02104-0\"},{\"title\":\"Gurobi: non-linear monomial · yalmip/YALMIP · Discussion #1076\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/yalmip/YALMIP/discussions/1076\"},{\"title\":\"Bilinear constraints and Gurobi?\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/yalmip/c/s_i3w1Arftg\"},{\"title\":\"Explicitly linearizing product of binary variables worsens performance – Gurobi Support Portal\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/community/posts/4409336457745-Explicitly-linearizing-product-of-binary-variables-worsens-performance\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Gurobi's RLT preprocessing for automatic linearization of bilinear products:\n\n## Automatic Linearization and Preprocessing\n\nGurobi offers special preprocessing, linearization, and cutting plane techniques to deal with products of variables. If at least one of the two variables in a product is binary, then the product can be modeled using a set of linear constraints.\n\nThe PreQLinearize parameter is no longer available, as Gurobi now automatically applies this parameter. This means Gurobi handles linearization decisions internally without requiring manual parameter tuning.\n\n## RLT (Reformulation Linearization Technique)\n\nGurobi version 9.0 includes cuts from the Reformulation Linearization Technique (RLT) and cuts for the Boolean Quadric Polytope (BQP). The reformulation–linearization technique (RLT) is a prominent approach to constructing tight linear relaxations of non-convex continuous and mixed-integer optimization problems, with the goal of extending applicability and improving performance for bilinear product relations.\n\n## Variable Product Detection\n\nA method for detecting bilinear product relations implicitly contained in mixed-integer linear programs analyzes linear constraints with binary variables, thus enabling the application of bilinear RLT to a new class of problems.\n\n## Important Note on Manual Linearization\n\nGurobi is able to use different reformulation techniques without explicit linearization, as the PreQLinearize parameter controls the reformulation technique, and manually linearizing bilinear terms can take away the possibility of applying a more efficient reformulation technique.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"5f228fa1-3bcc-4f4c-99a3-71b0a1c47690","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:25:57.744Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2e6f8e50-4680-405f-8e37-b062ae87f740","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
