{"parentUuid":"855d8fe5-22a2-4e49-9c26-6cde79191d1f","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a2dc46b9af8a17e14","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_016ZoePBsgzDCdWtxUnSZcfF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01W9svx9k7ywittUJfbYjYk4","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"Adams Sherali bilinear separation \"2024\" OR \"2025\" mixed integer cut implementation efficient"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1604,"cache_read_input_tokens":38047,"output_tokens":254,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1604},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":254,"cache_read_input_tokens":38047,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1604,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1604,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaozdiL1efJKGTETNZ5NB","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"1476a1d8-8265-494f-911d-6a03083eb22c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:26:14.849Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"1476a1d8-8265-494f-911d-6a03083eb22c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a2dc46b9af8a17e14","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W9svx9k7ywittUJfbYjYk4","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Adams Sherali bilinear separation \"2024\" OR \"2025\" mixed integer cut implementation efficient\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Efficient separation of RLT cuts for implicit and explicit bilinear terms | Mathematical Programming | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10107-024-02104-0\"},{\"title\":\"Efficient Separation of RLT Cuts for Implicit and Explicit Bilinear Products | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-32726-1_2\"},{\"title\":\"Reformulation–Linearization Techniques for Mixed-Discrete Optimization Problems | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/rwe/10.1007/978-1-4614-6624-6_45-1\"},{\"title\":\"Efficient Separation of RLT Cuts for Implicit and Explicit Bilinear Terms1footnote 11footnote 1This is the extended version of the article published as: Bestuzheva, K., Gleixner, A., Achterberg, T.: Efficient separation of RLT cuts for implicit and explicit bilinear products. In: Integer Programming and Combinatorial Optimization: 24th International Conference, IPCO 2023, Madison, WI, USA, June 21–23, 2023, Proceedings, pp. 14–28. Springer, Berlin, Heidelberg (2023). https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-32\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2211.13545\"},{\"title\":\"Mixed-integer bilinear programming problems | Mathematical Programming | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF01581249\"},{\"title\":\"Mixed-integer bilinear programming problems | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/Mixed-integer-bilinear-programming-problems-Adams-Sherali/2f931ef26f0c94a0472b535652b6e98345887057\"},{\"title\":\"A branch-and-cut algorithm for Mixed-Integer Bilinear Programming - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0377221719308008\"},{\"title\":\"Reformulation–Linearization Techniques for Discrete Optimization Problems | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/rwe/10.1007/978-1-4419-7997-1_45\"},{\"title\":\"Efficient separation of RLT cuts for implicit and explicit bilinear terms: Efficient separation of RLT cuts for implicit and explicit...: Mathematical Programming: Series A and B: Vol 210, No 1\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/abs/10.1007/s10107-024-02104-0\"},{\"title\":\"Efficient separation of RLT cuts for implicit and explicit bilinear terms | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/382315710_Efficient_separation_of_RLT_cuts_for_implicit_and_explicit_bilinear_terms\"}]\n\nI found relevant search results for your query. Here's a summary of the key findings:\n\n## Recent Publication on Efficient RLT Cut Separation\n\nA paper by Bestuzheva, Gleixner, and Achterberg on \"Efficient separation of RLT cuts for implicit and explicit bilinear terms\" was published in Mathematical Programming in 2025.\n\n## The Core Problem and Solution\n\nThe reformulation–linearization technique (RLT) is a prominent approach to constructing tight linear relaxations of non-convex continuous and mixed-integer optimization problems. The goal of this recent work is to extend the applicability and improve the performance of RLT for bilinear product relations.\n\n## Key Contributions\n\nThe paper addresses two main challenges:\n\n1. **Detection of Implicit Bilinear Relations**: A method for detecting bilinear product relations implicitly contained in mixed-integer linear programs, which is based on analyzing linear constraints with binary variables, thus enabling the application of bilinear RLT to a new class of problems.\n\n2. **Efficient Cut Separation**: A new RLT cutting plane separation algorithm addresses the high computational cost of RLT cut separation by proposing a method which identifies combinations of linear constraints and bound factors that are expected to yield violated inequalities.\n\n## Historical Context\n\nThe reformulation-linearization technique (RLT) was first proposed by Adams and Sherali for linearly constrained bilinear problems with binary variables, and has been applied to mixed-integer, semi-infinite, general bilinear and polynomial problems.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"57b44657-49bc-491f-bb6f-f1882336efd7","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:26:21.842Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1476a1d8-8265-494f-911d-6a03083eb22c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"57b44657-49bc-491f-bb6f-f1882336efd7","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a2dc46b9af8a17e14","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_019KwcmQWMBBLZ5j7xe8ndH2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Bbuz19WXHpV31TydvmM5py","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://arxiv.org/html/2211.13545","prompt":"Extract: (1) practical engineering complexity of separating RLT cuts, (2) computational results showing speedup or LP gap reduction, (3) which problem classes benefit most, (4) does it apply to 2D placement / packing / facility location-like problems with binary x ports + bilinear position products?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1959,"cache_read_input_tokens":39651,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1959,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":70,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaozeYk5ToGMyMPuJ7xG1","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"cb396b68-5b55-42a0-bb92-4ff6fd188156","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:26:26.978Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"cb396b68-5b55-42a0-bb92-4ff6fd188156","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a2dc46b9af8a17e14","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_019KwcmQWMBBLZ5j7xe8ndH2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UL6KwA74SwvPT389gEC1DN","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"\"Bestuzheva\" SCIP RLT cut bilinear MIP gap reduction performance benchmark"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1959,"cache_read_input_tokens":39651,"output_tokens":279,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1959},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":279,"cache_read_input_tokens":39651,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1959,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1959,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaozeYk5ToGMyMPuJ7xG1","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"52532108-9646-494b-ae26-2c471196dae4","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:26:27.218Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"52532108-9646-494b-ae26-2c471196dae4","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a2dc46b9af8a17e14","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UL6KwA74SwvPT389gEC1DN","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"Bestuzheva\" SCIP RLT cut bilinear MIP gap reduction performance benchmark\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Efficient Separation of RLT Cuts for Implicit and Explicit Bilinear Terms1footnote 11footnote 1This is the extended version of the article published as: Bestuzheva, K., Gleixner, A., Achterberg, T.: Efficient separation of RLT cuts for implicit and explicit bilinear products. In: Integer Programming and Combinatorial Optimization: 24th International Conference, IPCO 2023, Madison, WI, USA, June 21–23, 2023, Proceedings, pp. 14–28. Springer, Berlin, Heidelberg (2023). https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-32\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2211.13545\"},{\"title\":\"Efficient Separation of RLT Cuts for Implicit and Explicit Bilinear Products | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-32726-1_2\"},{\"title\":\"State-of-the-art Methods for Pseudo-Boolean Solving with SCIP\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2501.03390v1\"},{\"title\":\"Ksenia Bestuzheva's research works | Zuse Institute Berlin and other places\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/scientific-contributions/Ksenia-Bestuzheva-2130135125\"},{\"title\":\"Efficient separation of RLT cuts for implicit and explicit bilinear terms | Mathematical Programming | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10107-024-02104-0\"},{\"title\":\"The SCIP Optimization Suite 8.0 Ksenia Bestuzheva · Mathieu Besan¸con\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2112.08872\"},{\"title\":\"Efficient separation of RLT cuts for implicit and explicit bilinear terms | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/382315710_Efficient_separation_of_RLT_cuts_for_implicit_and_explicit_bilinear_terms\"},{\"title\":\"[2211.13545] Efficient Separation of RLT Cuts for Implicit and Explicit Bilinear Terms\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2211.13545\"},{\"title\":\"Efficient Separation of RLT Cuts for Implicit and Explicit Bilinear Products | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/370937028_Efficient_Separation_of_RLT_Cuts_for_Implicit_and_Explicit_Bilinear_Products\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Efficient Separation of RLT Cuts for Implicit and Explicit Bilinear Products\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/365783931_Efficient_Separation_of_RLT_Cuts_for_Implicit_and_Explicit_Bilinear_Products\"}]\n\nI found comprehensive research on this topic. Here's what the search results reveal:\n\n## Overview\n\nThe reformulation–linearization technique (RLT) is a prominent approach to constructing tight linear relaxations of non-convex continuous and mixed-integer optimization problems, with the goal being to extend applicability and improve performance of RLT for bilinear product relations.\n\n## Key Contributions by Bestuzheva et al.\n\nA method for detecting bilinear product relations implicitly contained in mixed-integer linear programs was developed, based on analyzing linear constraints with binary variables, thus enabling the application of bilinear RLT to a new class of problems.\n\nThe second contribution addresses the high computational cost of RLT cut separation, which presents a major difficulty in applying RLT efficiently in practice, proposing a new RLT cutting plane separation algorithm which identifies combinations of linear constraints and bound factors that are expected to yield inequalities violated by the current relaxation solution.\n\n## Performance Benchmarking\n\nA detailed computational study based on independent implementations in two solvers evaluates the performance impact of the proposed methods. Tables comparing settings Off, ERLT and IERLT on subsets of MILP and MINLP instances show time and nodes on instances where performance differences are significant.\n\n## Implementation Context\n\nSCIP generates RLT cutting planes for bilinear terms, including bilinear terms participating in nonlinear relations implicitly given by mixed-integer linear constraints. Where applicable, both Flower inequalities and RLT cuts significantly speed up the solving process.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"38c49aaa-b591-4ae9-a464-d64640962291","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:26:34.556Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"52532108-9646-494b-ae26-2c471196dae4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"cb396b68-5b55-42a0-bb92-4ff6fd188156","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a2dc46b9af8a17e14","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Bbuz19WXHpV31TydvmM5py","type":"tool_result","content":"# RLT Cuts for Bilinear Terms: Key Findings\n\n## (1) Practical Engineering Complexity of Separation\n\nThe paper identifies cut separation as \"one of the major difficulties in applying RLT efficiently in practice.\" The authors address this bottleneck through an efficient separation algorithm that leverages sign patterns of constraint coefficients and violation indicators to \"ignore combinations of factors that will not produce a violated inequality.\"\n\n## (2) Computational Results\n\nThe computational study (Section 5) demonstrates performance improvements through:\n- **Separation efficiency**: The proposed algorithm reduces computational cost of identifying RLT cuts\n- **Redundancy filtering**: Strategies for eliminating superfluous product relations improve performance\n- **Projection technique**: Constructing cuts from reduced constraint systems yields filtering benefits\n\nHowever, the abstract states results were \"evaluated...in two solvers\" with computational impact shown across different instance classes, though specific speedup percentages aren't quoted in the provided excerpt.\n\n## (3) Problem Classes Benefiting Most\n\nThe paper focuses on \"numerous applications whose models involve nonconvex quadratic nonlinearities\" and emphasizes binary variable interactions. The detection algorithm specifically targets problems where \"bilinear product relations...implicitly contained in mixed-integer linear programs\" exist—particularly those using big-M formulations with binary indicators.\n\n## (4) Applicability to Placement/Packing/Facility Location\n\n**The provided content does not address placement, packing, or facility location problems.** The paper focuses on general mixed-integer programs with explicit or implicit bilinear products, but contains no application-specific examples matching those problem classes."}]},"uuid":"ff6a0755-aacd-4429-9709-ee5ed7707ba9","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:26:37.128Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cb396b68-5b55-42a0-bb92-4ff6fd188156","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"ff6a0755-aacd-4429-9709-ee5ed7707ba9","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a2dc46b9af8a17e14","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01GiZETM4fBRuAY1LmdVTs3t","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"现在已有足够的资料。让我快速看一下我们项目的 master_model 代码确认 bilinear 项的具体形式。"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1633,"cache_creation_input_tokens":878,"cache_read_input_tokens":41610,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":878,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011Caozfg1Qx8PByfTm2cn16","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"59ec6d3b-8dd6-4b58-a67b-9820601d00f4","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:26:40.988Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
